; The overlay, on a world small enough to read in a sitting.
;
; A directory of its own, one level down from the build root, and both facts
; are load-bearing. Its own, because it is preprocessed by ppx_camlcast and
; dune's check context is per directory -- see test/ppx/dune, which learned
; that the hard way. One level down, because Camlcast.Asset looks beside the
; executable and one directory above it, and the font this draws with lives in
; assets/: an executable nested any deeper would not find it.
;
; Attached to no package, the way bench/ and examples/ are. `dune build`
; compiles it, so it cannot go stale against the library it demonstrates, and
; nothing installs it. It is deliberately not a demo/ catalogue entry either:
; adding one of those touches four places test_demos holds in sync, and this is
; dev-time tooling rather than an engine feature to show off.

(executable
 (name studio)
 (modules studio)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_camlcast))
 (libraries camlcast camlcast_core camlcast_edit))
